    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Locative with w, na and o",
     "texto": [
      "To say where something happens, **w** and **na** usually go with the locative: **w biurze**, **na rynku**. The topic of conversation comes with **o**: **o mieście**.",
      "The locative usually answers **gdzie?** («where?»). Don't confuse it with **dokąd?** («where to?»), which usually takes the accusative."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
